{"id": "EUVD-2026-55611", "enisaUuid": "e05621fb-b7bf-3b9f-b8f2-a2a63548fae1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nIB/mad: Drop unmatched RMPP responses before reassembly\n\nKernel-handled RMPP receive processing starts reassembly for active\nDATA responses before the response is matched to an outstanding send.\nThe normal match happens later, after ib_process_rmpp_recv_wc() has\neither assembled a complete message or consumed the segment.\n\nThat ordering lets an unsolicited response that routes to a kernel\nRMPP agent by the high TID bits allocate or extend RMPP receive state\nbefore the full TID and source address are checked against a real\nrequest. A reordered burst can therefore reach the receive-side\ninsertion path even though the response would not match any send.\n\nFor kernel-handled RMPP DATA responses, require the existing\nib_find_send_mad() match before entering RMPP reassembly. The matcher\nalready checks the full TID, management class and source address/GID\nagainst the agent wait, backlog and in-flight send lists. If there is\nno match, drop the response without creating RMPP state.\n\nThis leaves the RMPP window behavior unchanged and only rejects\nresponses that have no corresponding request.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45416c87ebcece1e90f3bc5bc172d106b77c6b69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9634fb1f4d404f36a20ffbcb8797369db69b06bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bfb9e8243fd2099d1080d09222964d988f991d9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dfa535c94406c03d3f0c869ef3ba5528e395737c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e1bd7f590b0ccfee07f7fe1d48b92059bd37d72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98d2d468b4faa1fdc68c0c6c238389906ee3490c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad9c9ad3204f63a46f0f7de29687a8e512f05e29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2e52d610b9b09694261632340b801a421e0b0c5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c7q4-7jj2-g2jh", "CVE-2026-68425"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20afb325-832f-3fec-809f-73107437ddbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <dfa535c94406c03d3f0c869ef3ba5528e395737c"}, {"id": "28534c2b-8a29-3e7d-a7c4-83b8c3e6205c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "2a2b7f36-80d3-39ef-a4d2-ae167fe30f2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "35ec5f21-9621-3161-986c-f2be4f0cd079", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <9634fb1f4d404f36a20ffbcb8797369db69b06bb"}, {"id": "5219ec88-397f-344e-9b04-36e7bfbcec8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "7a0b0e0d-7d31-3904-b9aa-511ff3870fa8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "93d34278-9700-3cab-9e78-cb5a957dcbdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "9b822ae2-3445-370a-ba28-df334a92cc20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <98d2d468b4faa1fdc68c0c6c238389906ee3490c"}, {"id": "abda2791-25c4-3048-8d37-971314fb5492", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "b3a17ade-0491-3ace-b737-db45f61cfca6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <ad9c9ad3204f63a46f0f7de29687a8e512f05e29"}, {"id": "c0147c50-d917-3dc7-94d0-7d7a498f2c1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "ce78eac7-ce1b-3a54-8339-2d9a37fc8909", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <45416c87ebcece1e90f3bc5bc172d106b77c6b69"}, {"id": "d0d93db7-fda4-3e66-9516-a3a413dd72e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <d2e52d610b9b09694261632340b801a421e0b0c5"}, {"id": "d59b5c42-0114-3b2e-b0d1-4a2f51c1e798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <bfb9e8243fd2099d1080d09222964d988f991d9b"}, {"id": "d623166b-a8f3-327d-8004-032a786ae5a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa619a77046bef30478697aba0553991033afb8e <6e1bd7f590b0ccfee07f7fe1d48b92059bd37d72"}, {"id": "dd8b421c-84fb-32be-842f-0b60b64757ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.13"}, {"id": "ea67b5e1-4973-36dc-895e-9849ee76a88c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f8a61b7b-1d02-3e1f-a942-d62c847dd018", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "16a78970-6815-379e-a959-21dd6283d2f6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}